# jev — jev

The local Jev decision engine: index a corpus, narrow it for FREE with keyless verbs, then ask a calibrated question about the survivors. USE THIS BEFORE DECIDING ANYTHING THAT IS A JUDGEMENT — classification, prioritisation, is-this-X, should-I-Y, which-of-N, how-confident — and BEFORE reading many files to find the few that matter. VERBS: index (build/refresh, keyless) · query (FTS/where, keyless) · scan (keyword+excerpt, keyless) · cluster (signature groups, keyless) · extract (regex -> structured rows, keyless) · report (index state, keyless) · filter (JUDGED narrowing with probabilities) · find (JUDGED 9-stage pattern chain) · decision-tree (JUDGED batch classification from a recipe) · route (JUDGED tool selection) · evaluate (JUDGED calibration) · push-gate / st-detect / spec-audit (mechanical gates). THE JUDGE IS LOCAL AND FREE — no api key, no billing, no quota; ~100ms warm, ~22s for 100 candidates in ONE request. ASK ONE THING: a compound 'X or Y' question caps the score below 0.5 and clears no real threshold. Sweep the threshold and read max/spread before you trust a min_p. READ THE TREND on find: 'N judged · 1 request' is healthy; 'N requests' means the endpoint is the llama.cpp backend, not the adapter.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** index|query|scan|cluster|extract|report|target|watch (keyless) | filter|find|decision-tree|route|evaluate (judged) | push-gate|st-detect|spec-audit (gates) */
  verb: "index" | "query" | "scan" | "cluster" | "extract" | "report" | "target" | "watch" | "filter" | "find" | "decision-tree" | "route" | "evaluate" | "push-gate" | "st-detect" | "spec-audit";
  /** one line: what you are looking for and why */
  i?: string;
  /** index name (query/scan/cluster/extract/filter/report) */
  index?: string;
  /** FTS5 MATCH phrase, e.g. theatrical or "exact phrase" */
  fts?: string;
  /** SQL predicate on the files row, e.g. size>20000 */
  where?: string;
  /** keyword for scan/cluster (excerpts returned) */
  lex?: string;
  /** regex for scan/cluster/extract */
  re?: string;
  /** JSON field to pull (extract from jsonl/sqlite) */
  field?: string;
  /** filter/route: ONE specific claim. Compound 'X or Y' questions score mid-range and clear nothing — state a single thing the text either is or is not */
  question?: string;
  /** find: the X to hunt across the corpus */
  phrase?: string;
  /** find: minimum support n for a pattern (default 2) */
  common?: number;
  /** decision threshold. DERIVE it: sweep 0.2/0.4/0.6/0.8 and read max + spread. max < 0.5 means the QUESTION is broken, not the threshold */
  min_p?: number;
  /** max rows (query/scan/filter) */
  limit?: number;
  /** index: path or @target to ingest */
  target?: string;
  /** target subcommand argument */
  path?: string;
  /** decision-tree: rows file (json array or jsonl) */
  rows?: string;
  /** decision-tree: recipe file */
  recipe?: string;
  /** decision-tree: where to write the decisions */
  out?: string;
  /** machine-readable stdout (stderr carries the cost line) */
  json?: boolean;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://jev.

